 "generatorWeaknesses": [
  "ENTITY words cover only through concept.entity: no concept names fish or salmon as an entity, so LOOK_AT_ENTITY cod with the word 물고기 validates only because an IN_BIOME condition on a biome tag always counts as a mention (GoalType.covers: BIOME id starting with '#'). wasserpfad and brandung use that. IN_WATER does not count, so 'underwater, watch a fish' cannot teach 물고기.",
  "WaveQaTest builds generated hints with a stub namer: a covered object that is not the concept's own item (yellow_carpet for 양탄자, birch_sapling for 묘목, spruce_door for 문, a raw beef input) never contains the taught word, so those steps carry an authored hint.",
  "BUILD_PATTERN RING and PLACE_ON_PATTERN on a ring speak 울타리: the house walls of dorfhaus read '판자 울타리 옆에 문을 달아요' and the clue for the bed is authored ('새 집 안에 침대를 놓아요'). The ceremony line of dorfhaus is authored for the same reason (generated: '참나무 판자 울타리 안에 침대를 놓았어요').",
  "The sentence for a covered block or item uses the registry name for non-first items in PLACE_REL / PLACE_ON_PATTERN / CRAFT: '문 앞에 노란색 양탄자를 깔아요', '물 옆에 자작나무 묘목을 심어요', '노란색 염료를 만들어요' (the last needs the generated concept gen_yellow_dye as taught word).",
  "PLACE_BLOCK on a torch still reads 횃불을 밝혀요 and the HOLD_WHILE finale takes the inner verb for the (verb, object) pair, so HOLD_WHILE torch + PLACE counted as (PLACE, torch) for variety.verbObjectMax; lavapfad uses a HOLDING condition instead.",
  "A tool the learner must hold (shears for seagrass and carved pumpkins, a fishing rod, wheat for the goat) costs a second unknown word in the clue; the batch keeps the clue to one new word and names the tool in an authored hint.",
  "REACH_BIOME always says '~로 가요', which makes 가다 an unknown word at the very first trails; wasserpfad and schildkroete author '도착해요' (ARRIVE) so their first sentence has one unknown word.",
  "There is no generated sentence for 이야기하다 that does not use INTERACT_ENTITY on a villager, and (TALK, villager) is already at 2 pairs; handelspfad s2 is an authored two-sentence clue on a GIVE step ('주민과 이야기해요. 감자를 줘요.').",
  "Pair slack: (STACK, cobblestone), (PLACE, campfire), (EAT, carrot), (STACK, snow_block), (WATCH, rabbit) and (CRAFT, red_dye) already stand at 3, and a pile of other pairs at 2; the batch only uses pairs that end at 2 and picks bed, carpet, banner and dye colours that nobody used (blue_bed, green_bed, yellow_carpet, red_banner, yellow_dye).",
  "Seagrass cannot be taught without two unknown words in the finale (거북에게 해초를 줘요): two new nouns in one sentence need three earlier encounters each."
 ]
}
